course: dictionary
lesson: 15589
title: Natural or synthetic?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word synthetic is about where something comes from. Most of the time it means made by people, usually from chemicals in a factory, not grown or found in nature. «The jacket is made from synthetic fibre, not wool.»
explain: Look at the clues around the word. If the sentence mentions chemicals, factories or materials like nylon, synthetic means made by people. If it talks about flavours or diamonds that are not real, synthetic means fake or artificial.
explain: Try the swap test. Put «made by people» or «fake» into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «Synthetic grass» is grass made in a factory, so it does not grow in the ground. Its opposite is natural.
fact: Synthetic means made by people from chemicals or in a factory, not grown or found in nature.
fact: Synthetic can also mean fake or artificial, as in «synthetic flavours» or «synthetic diamonds».
fact: Synthetics are synthetic materials or fabrics, such as nylon, polyester and acrylic.
fact: Natural materials include wool, cotton and wood. Synthetic materials include nylon, polyester and plastics.
fact: Scientists compare natural and synthetic materials, for example how strong they are and whether they let water through.
exercise: «The jacket was made from synthetic fibre, not wool.» What does synthetic mean here? | Grown on a farm | Very old | Found under a river | *Made by people from chemicals, not from nature
exercise: Ella reads «synthetic flavours» on a sweet packet. What does synthetic suggest? | Fresh from the garden | Made of wool | *Fake or artificial, not natural | Sour and bitter
exercise: Which material is synthetic? | Wool | Wood | *Nylon | Cotton
test: What does synthetic mean in «synthetic grass»? | Grass that is cut very short | Grass that grows naturally in a field | *Grass made in a factory from plastic-like materials | Grass that is dried to make hay
test: Which one is a natural material? | Plastic | Polyester | Acrylic | *Cotton
exam: Mia says, «The sofa is covered in synthetic leather.» What does Mia tell us about the sofa? | It is very old and ancient | *Its covering was made by people from chemicals, not from an animal | It is covered in real animal skin | It grew in the garden like a plant
